# iyi: the chaos scheduler - SPEC.md III.4.17. Required only by a build
# with `-Diyi_chaos`, which is what `iyi test --chaos` makes, so a program
# built without it carries none of this: no field, no branch, no call.
#
# The compiler rules out memory races (III.4.4), which leaves one kind of
# concurrency bug a test can pass by luck: a logical ordering race, where
# the program is right only because its tasks happened to run in one
# order - a check of an `Atomic` and the act on it with another task
# between them, a value read before the task that writes it was joined.
# Here the runtime's scheduling choices are made from a seeded stream,
# so a test run over many seeds meets many orders, and a seed that fails
# names its schedule: run again with it, it fails the same way.
#
# **What is chosen.** With `IYI_WORKERS=1`, which `iyi test --chaos` sets,
# every task runs on the program's one thread and the schedule is the
# stream's alone ("simulated" below):
#
#   - which ready task runs next, at every park (`pick`);
#   - whether the running task is preempted at a synchronising operation:
#     an `Atomic`'s verb (std/atomic's and std/mutex's included, through
#     the prelude's `Atomic`), a channel's send, receive, close, select or
#     non-blocking half, a spawn and a task's `value` (`point`);
#   - whether it is preempted at a loop's back-edge, on a countdown drawn
#     from the stream (`back_edge`);
#   - which task parked on a word a wake readies, and in what order
#     (`IyiScheduler.chaos_wake_on`), which is std/mutex's hand-over;
#   - which arm of a `select` is tried first when more than one is ready
#     (`arm`).
#
# A task the compiler would run in parallel (a `spawn` it placed on the
# pool, `spawn(unit: :new)`) runs on this thread as a unit of its own
# (`IyiChaosUnit`), and a `Unit`'s tasks (std/unit, `spawn(in:)`) as that
# `Unit`'s one chaos unit, so the interleavings two cores could produce
# are the ones met here: tasks of different units take turns at any of
# the points above. Tasks of one unit still take turns only at parks,
# oldest first, as the language promises them (III.4.18): the scheduler
# never puts a task between two operations of a unit-mate.
#
# Every synchronising operation is a point because the compiler's rule
# makes that enough: a program with no data race behaves as some
# interleaving of its synchronising operations (the DRF-SC theorem, and
# `Atomic` has one ordering, sequentially consistent - III.4.10), so a
# switch between two plain reads can show nothing a switch at the next
# operation could not.
#
# **Two strategies, chosen by the seed.** Half the seeds walk at random:
# at each point the running task is preempted with a probability of one
# in 2, 4, 8 or 16, and a choice of task is uniform over the units that
# may run. The other half are PCT (Burckhardt, Kothari, Musuvathi and
# Nagarakatte, "A Randomized Scheduler with Probabilistic Guarantees of
# Finding Bugs", ASPLOS 2010): each unit gets a random priority, the
# highest that may run always runs, and at d - 1 steps drawn from the
# first k the running unit drops below every other - which finds a bug of
# depth d in one run of n·k^(d-1) at worst. d is 1, 2 or 3 and k a power
# of two from 8 to 16,384, drawn per seed, since a run's length is not
# known before it ends. A unit that stays highest through 1,024 steps in
# a row - a spin waiting for a lower one - is dropped below the rest, or
# PCT would starve the task it waits for.
#
# **Reproducible, and what is not.** Simulated, the schedule is a function
# of the seed and of what the program does: no decision reads a clock, an
# address or another thread. What a program reads from outside is not
# the seed's: a sleep or a timeout ends when the clock says, an I/O
# wait when the kernel answers, and a thread of the program's own
# (`IyiThread.start`) runs beside this one, not in its schedule. A run
# whose order turns on those can differ with the same seed. With
# `IYI_WORKERS` above 1 the pool's threads are real ("threads" below):
# each draws from a stream of its own, seeded from the seed and the order
# the threads first drew, to pick the worker a steal starts at, to give a
# parallel task's worker up at a point or at a back-edge the monitor
# flagged, to order a `select`'s arms and a word's wakes - more orders
# than the plain pool meets, and no promise of meeting one again.
#
# `IYI_CHAOS=SEED` turns it on in a build that has it; `IYI_CHAOS_TRACE`
# set as well prints, as the program ends, the seed, the strategy and the
# schedule's hash - a fold of every choice made - which is how
# bench/chaos_exercise.sh shows two runs of one seed took one schedule.
@[Unsafe("the chaos scheduler reads the runtime's thread words and writes its trace through raw memory")]
{% if flag?(:gc_none) || flag?(:gc_boehm) %}
  {% raise "-Diyi_chaos needs the default runtime: its scheduler is the one a chaos build drives, and -Dgc_none and -Dgc_boehm have no pool to simulate (SPEC.md III.4.17)" %}
{% end %}

# A unit as the chaos scheduler sees it (SPEC.md III.4.18): the tasks
# that take turns only at parks - the main thread's, a parallel task's
# and the tasks its block spawns in its unit, or a `Unit`'s. Its PCT
# priority, and the mark a choice puts on it
# so that one walk of the run queue finds each unit's candidate.
class IyiChaosUnit
  getter id : UInt64
  property priority : UInt64
  property stamp : UInt64
  property slot : Int32

  def initialize(@id : UInt64, @priority : UInt64)
    @stamp = 0_u64
    @slot = 0
  end
end

# heap22: the runtime's unit a simulated parallel task runs in
# (`IyiGroup#chaos_task`), marked so: its token is the simulation's
# thread's for good, and its fibers run there alone, whichever thread
# wakes them (`IyiScheduler.ready`).
class IyiUnit
  @chaos_kept : Bool = false
  property chaos_kept : Bool
end

class IyiGroup
  # :nodoc: — a task the compiler or the program put on the pool
  # (`spawn_pooled`, `on_pool`), simulated: kept on this thread as a unit
  # of its own (`IyiChaos.parallel_task`). Under heap22's partitions it is
  # a unit of the runtime's as well, with a partition of its own unless
  # *pinned* (design section 4.5), and its crossing is made as `pooled`
  # makes a pool unit's: the block's captures and the group published,
  # the unit, the fiber, the task, its box and the closure the fiber runs
  # made in the shared heap. Made by `in_unit` in the spawner's partition
  # and published after, the glue was the spawner's, which heap_crossings'
  # `glue` check named (simulated, Linux). Without partitions it is a task
  # of its spawner's unit, as it was before heap22.
  private def chaos_task(pinned : Bool, &block : -> T) : IyiTask(T) forall T
    # Named outside the `{% if %}`: a block parameter read only inside one
    # is not captured. A no-op without partitions (`IyiCross`).
    IyiCross.publish(block)
    {% if flag?(:heap_partitions) %}
      raise "a task spawned on a group whose block has ended: no scope is left to join it" if @ended
      IyiScheduler.make_stacks_with { |fresh| fresh.prepare_stack } unless IyiScheduler.makes_stacks?
      IyiCross.publish(self)
      unit = IyiCross.shared { IyiUnit.new(pinned: pinned) }
      # Its token held by this thread for good, as the worker running a
      # pool unit holds it: no idle worker's takeover collects its
      # partition while the simulation runs one of its fibers. And its
      # fibers kept here: a program that sizes the pool (`IyiWorkers.count
      # = 4`) or starts a thread makes the scheduler shared, and `ready`
      # would push a fiber of a unit onto the pool, whose workers find its
      # token held and leave it on the unit's list for good -
      # heap_crossings' `in` and `unit_new`, simulated, named a deadlock
      # every seed (Linux).
      unit.take(IyiScheduler.state.object_id)
      unit.chaos_kept = true
      task = IyiCross.shared do
        fiber = IyiFiber.new
        fiber.home = IyiScheduler.state
        fiber.unit = unit
        crossing_task(fiber, block)
      end
      IyiScheduler.enqueue(task.fiber)
      IyiChaos.parallel_task(task)
    {% else %}
      IyiChaos.parallel_task(in_unit(&block))
    {% end %}
  end
end

class IyiChaos
  # `@@mode`: not read yet, off (a chaos build run without `IYI_CHAOS`),
  # the one-thread simulation, or real threads.
  UNREAD    = 0
  OFF       = 1
  SIMULATED = 2
  THREADS   = 3

  # splitmix64's increment, and FNV-1a's offset basis and prime.
  GOLDEN    = 0x9E3779B97F4A7C15_u64
  FNV_BASIS = 0xCBF29CE484222325_u64
  FNV_PRIME =      0x100000001B3_u64

  # PCT's priorities: a unit's first is above `HIGH`; the i-th change
  # point drops the running unit to `LOW + d - i`; a unit dropped for
  # spinning goes below that, one under the last one dropped.
  HIGH       = 0x10000000000_u64
  LOW        =      0x100000_u64
  SPIN_STEPS =          1024_u64

  @@mode : Int32 = 0
  @@seed : UInt64 = 0_u64
  @@stream : UInt64 = 0_u64
  @@pct : Bool = false
  @@odds : UInt64 = 2_u64
  @@depth : UInt64 = 1_u64
  @@horizon : UInt64 = 8_u64
  @@change_one : UInt64 = 0_u64
  @@change_two : UInt64 = 0_u64
  @@changed : UInt64 = 0_u64
  @@floor : UInt64 = 0_u64
  @@edge_mean : UInt64 = 16_u64
  @@edge_left : UInt64 = 1_u64
  @@steps : UInt64 = 0_u64
  @@yields : UInt64 = 0_u64
  @@picks : UInt64 = 0_u64
  @@schedule : UInt64 = 0_u64
  @@units : UInt64 = 0_u64
  @@root : IyiChaosUnit?
  @@last_unit : UInt64 = 0_u64
  @@streak : UInt64 = 0_u64
  @@candidates : Array(IyiFiber)?
  @@generation : UInt64 = 0_u64
  @@trace : Bool = false
  @@reported : Bool = false
  @@threads_seen : UInt64 = 0_u64
  # `IYI_CHAOS_LATE_THREADS`: a thread the simulated thread starts links
  # itself late (`hold_start`, `wait_late`); 1 in `@@late_closed` while
  # one waits, `@@late_steps` the points and back-edges passed since.
  LATE_STEPS = 1024_u64
  @@late_threads : Bool = false
  @@late_closed : UInt64 = 0_u64
  @@late_steps : UInt64 = 0_u64
  # The thread the simulation runs on: the main thread, which `start`
  # marks before the program's first line.
  @[ThreadLocal]
  @@here : Bool = false
  @[ThreadLocal]
  @@thread_stream : UInt64 = 0_u64
  @[ThreadLocal]
  @@thread_seeded : Bool = false

  # Read once, on the main thread, before the program's own code runs
  # (`__iyi_program`): the seed, the strategy it draws, and on one worker
  # the back-edge word raised for good on this thread, so that every
  # checked loop calls `back_edge`.
  def self.start : Nil
    return unless @@mode == UNREAD
    text = Program.env("IYI_CHAOS")
    unless text.is_a?(String) && text.bytesize > 0
      @@mode = OFF
      return
    end
    @@seed = seed_of(text)
    @@stream = @@seed
    @@schedule = FNV_BASIS
    @@trace = Program.env("IYI_CHAOS_TRACE").is_a?(String)
    @@late_threads = Program.env("IYI_CHAOS_LATE_THREADS").is_a?(String)
    @@here = true
    # Every parameter from the stream, so a seed names all of them.
    @@pct = draw % 2_u64 == 1_u64
    @@odds = 2_u64.unsafe_shl(draw % 4_u64)
    @@depth = 1_u64 &+ draw % 3_u64
    @@horizon = 8_u64.unsafe_shl(draw % 12_u64)
    @@change_one = 1_u64 &+ draw % @@horizon
    @@change_two = 1_u64 &+ draw % @@horizon
    @@floor = LOW
    @@edge_mean = 16_u64.unsafe_shl(draw % 7_u64)
    @@edge_left = 1_u64 &+ draw % (@@edge_mean &* 2_u64)
    fold(@@pct ? 1_u64 : 0_u64)
    fold(@@odds)
    fold(@@depth)
    fold(@@horizon)
    @@root = IyiChaosUnit.new(0_u64, fresh_priority)
    if IyiWorkers.resolved == 1
      @@mode = SIMULATED
      IyiWorkers.chaos_raise
    else
      @@mode = THREADS
    end
  end

  # The seed as the decimal number it is written as, wrapping past 64
  # bits; anything else is refused by name rather than read as 0.
  private def self.seed_of(text : String) : UInt64
    bytes = text.to_unsafe
    value = 0_u64
    index = 0
    while index < text.bytesize
      digit = bytes[index]
      unless digit >= 48_u8 && digit <= 57_u8
        raise "IYI_CHAOS is a seed, a decimal number, not '#{text}' (SPEC.md III.4.17)"
      end
      value = value &* 10_u64 &+ (digit - 48_u8).to_u64
      index = index + 1
    end
    value
  end

  # Whether this thread's schedule is the simulation's.
  def self.simulated? : Bool
    @@mode == SIMULATED && @@here
  end

  def self.active? : Bool
    @@mode >= SIMULATED
  end

  # The one source of every choice: splitmix64 over the seed on the
  # simulated thread, over the thread's own stream elsewhere. A draw of 0
  # is the plain scheduler's choice at every call site below - the head of
  # the run queue, no preemption, the first arm, the oldest waiter - which
  # is what bench/chaos_exercise.sh's copy with the stream ignored shows.
  def self.draw : UInt64
    if @@mode == SIMULATED && @@here
      state = @@stream &+ GOLDEN
      @@stream = state
      return mix(state)
    end
    unless @@thread_seeded
      ordinal = Pointer(Atomic(UInt64)).new(pointerof(@@threads_seen).address).value.add(1_u64)
      @@thread_stream = @@seed ^ mix(ordinal &+ 1_u64)
      @@thread_seeded = true
    end
    state = @@thread_stream &+ GOLDEN
    @@thread_stream = state
    mix(state)
  end

  def self.mix(word : UInt64) : UInt64
    z = word
    z = (z ^ z.unsafe_shr(30_u64)) &* 0xBF58476D1CE4E5B9_u64
    z = (z ^ z.unsafe_shr(27_u64)) &* 0x94D049BB133111EB_u64
    z ^ z.unsafe_shr(31_u64)
  end

  # A number below *bound*, from the stream.
  def self.below(bound : Int32) : Int32
    (draw % bound.to_u64).to_i32
  end

  private def self.fold(value : UInt64) : Nil
    @@schedule = (@@schedule ^ value) &* FNV_PRIME
  end

  private def self.fresh_priority : UInt64
    HIGH &+ (draw & 0xFFFFFFFF_u64)
  end

  # The unit *fiber* takes turns in; a fiber made before it had one - the
  # main fiber - is the root unit's.
  def self.unit_of(fiber : IyiFiber) : IyiChaosUnit
    unit = fiber.chaos_unit
    return unit if unit.is_a?(IyiChaosUnit)
    root = @@root
    root = IyiCross.shared { IyiChaosUnit.new(0_u64, HIGH) } unless root.is_a?(IyiChaosUnit)
    @@root = root
    fiber.chaos_unit = root
    root
  end

  # A task spawned into its spawner's unit (`IyiGroup#in_unit`).
  def self.adopt(fiber : IyiFiber) : Nil
    return unless simulated?
    fiber.chaos_unit = unit_of(IyiScheduler.current)
  end

  # A task the compiler or the program put on the pool, kept on this
  # thread as a unit of its own (`IyiGroup#chaos_task`); and a point at
  # once, since such a task may start beside its spawner.
  def self.parallel_task(task : IyiTask(T)) : IyiTask(T) forall T
    @@units = @@units &+ 1_u64
    # The shared heap's, as the fibers that name it are (heap22 row 14).
    task.fiber.chaos_unit = IyiCross.shared { IyiChaosUnit.new(@@units, fresh_priority) }
    point
    task
  end

  # Whether *fiber* is a fiber of a simulated parallel task's unit, which
  # runs on the simulation's thread alone.
  def self.kept?(fiber : IyiFiber) : Bool
    unit = fiber.unit
    unit.is_a?(IyiUnit) && unit.chaos_kept
  end

  # A task of a `Unit` (`IyiGroup#on_main`), simulated: in that `Unit`'s
  # chaos unit, made at its first task, so its tasks take turns with each
  # other only at parks and with every other unit at any point.
  def self.adopt_into(fiber : IyiFiber, owner : IyiGroup::Unit(S)) : Nil forall S
    return unless @@mode == SIMULATED
    unit = owner.iyi_chaos_unit
    unless unit.is_a?(IyiChaosUnit)
      @@units = @@units &+ 1_u64
      unit = IyiCross.shared { IyiChaosUnit.new(@@units, fresh_priority) }
      owner.iyi_chaos_unit = unit
    end
    fiber.chaos_unit = unit
  end

  # ── Points ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  # A synchronising operation is about to run: maybe another unit first.
  # Inside `Atomic`'s verbs this is `at_atomic`, which the compiler drops
  # from the copy of them the runtime calls (`CodeGenVisitor#visit(Call)`):
  # the runtime's own atomics are its locks and queues, and a switch inside
  # one would park a task holding them.
  def self.point : Nil
    # heap22's stress and false words (heap_verify.iyi) first, on the
    # task that reached the point.
    {% if flag?(:heap_verify) && flag?(:heap_partitions) %}
      IyiHeapVerify.at_point
    {% end %}
    mode = @@mode
    if mode == SIMULATED
      if @@here
        late_tick if @@late_closed != 0_u64
        step(false)
      end
    elsif mode == THREADS
      thread_point
    end
  end

  def self.at_atomic : Nil
    point
  end

  # One step of the simulation: counted, PCT's change points applied, and
  # the running task preempted when the strategy says so. Not before a
  # second unit exists, since a task preempted holding the only unit runs
  # again at once; not while the program is ending, nor in a fiber the
  # runtime is moving, nor with the scheduler's lock or the runtime's lock
  # held. A std loop that runs under the runtime's lock still reaches its
  # back-edges here (`GC.stats`, std/gc.iyi), and a park there waited on
  # the lock its own thread held: under `IYI_HEAP_STRESS` the collection
  # at the park spun in `IyiRuntimeLock.lock` for ever (std_http_exercise,
  # seed 3, one worker, every machine), as `thread_point` already knew.
  # A back-edge's step (*edge*) is computing, not waiting, so it does not
  # count towards PCT's spin.
  private def self.step(edge : Bool) : Nil
    return if @@units == 0_u64
    fiber = IyiScheduler.current
    return unless fiber.state == IyiFiberState::Running
    return if IyiScheduler.exiting? || IyiSchedLock.held_here? || IyiRuntimeLock.held?
    unit = unit_of(fiber)
    @@steps = @@steps &+ 1_u64
    if unit.id != @@last_unit
      @@last_unit = unit.id
      @@streak = 0_u64
    elsif !edge
      @@streak = @@streak &+ 1_u64
    end
    if @@pct
      steps = @@steps
      if @@changed &+ 1_u64 < @@depth && (steps == @@change_one || steps == @@change_two)
        @@changed = @@changed &+ 1_u64
        unit.priority = LOW &+ @@depth &- @@changed
      end
      if @@streak >= SPIN_STEPS
        drop(unit)
        # A unit that spins waits for something: a sleeper whose time has
        # come and the poller's news join the run queue here, as an OS's
        # timer lets them in. Without it the run queue was looked at only
        # where a task parks, and a task spinning for a unit asleep in
        # `sleep(1)` outranked nothing for ever (heap_crossings' ring
        # check on tmac, seeds 1 and 2, under `IYI_HEAP_STRESS`).
        IyiScheduler.poll_now(IyiScheduler.state)
      end
      return unless outranked?(IyiScheduler.state, unit)
    else
      return unless draw % @@odds == @@odds &- 1_u64
    end
    @@yields = @@yields &+ 1_u64
    fold(0xFFFFFFFF00000000_u64 | @@steps)
    fiber.chaos_held = true
    IyiScheduler.enqueue(fiber)
    IyiScheduler.reschedule
  end

  # PCT: below every unit there is, for a unit that ran too long alone.
  private def self.drop(unit : IyiChaosUnit) : Nil
    @@floor = @@floor &- 1_u64
    unit.priority = @@floor
    @@streak = 0_u64
  end

  # PCT: whether a unit other than *unit* waits with a higher priority.
  private def self.outranked?(st : IyiSchedulerState, unit : IyiChaosUnit) : Bool
    walk = st.run_head
    while walk.is_a?(IyiFiber)
      other = unit_of(walk)
      return true if other.id != unit.id && other.priority > unit.priority
      walk = walk.next_run
    end
    false
  end

  # A loop's back-edge on the simulated thread, whose word stays raised:
  # one step once the countdown drawn from the stream runs out. True when
  # it was the simulation's, so `IyiWorkers.preempted` does nothing more.
  def self.back_edge : Bool
    return false unless @@mode == SIMULATED && @@here
    late_tick if @@late_closed != 0_u64
    return true if @@units == 0_u64
    left = @@edge_left
    if left > 1_u64
      @@edge_left = left &- 1_u64
      return true
    end
    @@edge_left = 1_u64 &+ draw % (@@edge_mean &* 2_u64)
    step(true)
    true
  end

  # ── Choosing the next task ───────────────────────────────────────────

  # The next fiber this thread runs, out of its run queue: the plain
  # queue's head off the simulation, and on it one unit's candidate - the
  # fiber preempted holding the unit, or else the unit's oldest - chosen
  # at random, or by PCT's priority.
  def self.pick(st : IyiSchedulerState) : IyiFiber?
    return IyiScheduler.dequeue(st) unless @@mode == SIMULATED && @@here
    head = st.run_head
    return nil unless head.is_a?(IyiFiber)
    candidates = @@candidates
    unless candidates.is_a?(Array(IyiFiber))
      candidates = Array(IyiFiber).new(16)
      @@candidates = candidates
    end
    generation = @@generation &+ 1_u64
    @@generation = generation
    count = 0
    walk = head
    while walk.is_a?(IyiFiber)
      unit = unit_of(walk)
      if unit.stamp != generation
        unit.stamp = generation
        unit.slot = count
        if count < candidates.size
          candidates[count] = walk
        else
          candidates << walk
        end
        count = count + 1
      elsif walk.chaos_held
        candidates[unit.slot] = walk
      end
      walk = walk.next_run
    end
    chosen = candidates[0]
    if count > 1
      if @@pct
        # A unit picked again and again at its own parks - a spin on
        # `sleep(0)` - drops as one spinning on an operation does.
        if @@streak >= SPIN_STEPS
          index = 0
          while index < count
            spinner = unit_of(candidates[index])
            drop(spinner) if spinner.id == @@last_unit
            index = index + 1
          end
        end
        best = 0
        index = 1
        while index < count
          best = index if unit_of(candidates[index]).priority > unit_of(candidates[best]).priority
          index = index + 1
        end
        chosen = candidates[best]
      else
        chosen = candidates[below(count)]
      end
      @@picks = @@picks &+ 1_u64
      fold(unit_of(chosen).id)
      fold(count.to_u64)
    end
    take_out(st, chosen)
    chosen.chaos_held = false
    unit = unit_of(chosen)
    if unit.id == @@last_unit
      @@streak = @@streak &+ 1_u64
    else
      @@last_unit = unit.id
      @@streak = 0_u64
    end
    chosen
  end

  private def self.take_out(st : IyiSchedulerState, chosen : IyiFiber) : Nil
    previous : IyiFiber? = nil
    walk = st.run_head
    while walk.is_a?(IyiFiber)
      if walk.object_id == chosen.object_id
        following = walk.next_run
        if previous.is_a?(IyiFiber)
          previous.next_run = following
        else
          st.run_head = following
        end
        st.run_tail = previous if following.is_a?(Nil)
        walk.next_run = nil
        return
      end
      previous = walk
      walk = walk.next_run
    end
  end

  # ── The rest of the choices ──────────────────────────────────────────

  # The arm of a `select` over *arms* tried first, or -1 off chaos.
  def self.arm(arms : Int32) : Int32
    return -1 unless active?
    return -1 if @@mode == SIMULATED && !@@here
    below(arms)
  end

  # Whether a wake on a word chooses its waiters (`chaos_wake_on`).
  def self.chooses_wakes? : Bool
    return false unless active?
    @@mode == THREADS || @@here
  end

  # The worker a steal starts looking at, or -1 for the pool's own turn.
  def self.steal_start(count : Int64) : Int64
    return -1_i64 unless @@mode == THREADS
    (draw % count.to_u64).to_i64
  end

  # Real threads: a parallel task's worker given up, at a point and at a
  # back-edge the monitor flagged, one time in the seed's odds. Anywhere
  # else a point gives the core up instead: a fiber of a thread outside
  # the pool takes turns with its thread's others only at parks.
  private def self.thread_point : Nil
    return unless draw % @@odds == @@odds &- 1_u64
    st = IyiScheduler.state
    fiber = IyiScheduler.current
    return unless fiber.state == IyiFiberState::Running
    return if IyiScheduler.exiting? || IyiSchedLock.held_here? || IyiRuntimeLock.held?
    root = st.root
    if st.worker && fiber.unit.is_a?(IyiUnit) && !fiber.homebound && !(root.is_a?(IyiFiber) && root.object_id == fiber.object_id)
      IyiWorkers.chaos_give_up(st, fiber)
    else
      IyiThread.yield_cpu
    end
  end

  def self.forced_turn? : Bool
    @@mode == THREADS && draw % @@odds == @@odds &- 1_u64
  end

  # ── A thread that links itself late ──────────────────────────────────
  #
  # A thread started on darwin, and on Linux when libc made it, links and
  # counts itself only once it runs (`IyiThread.run`): until then only
  # `IyiThread.others_started?` sees it, and how long that lasts is the
  # OS's choice, not the seed's - on tmac the threads'-list-only copy of
  # `Mutex.alone?` deadlocked on seeds 5-7 and was answered on 1-4 and 8.
  # With `IYI_CHAOS_LATE_THREADS` set, a thread the simulated thread
  # starts waits to link itself until that thread has nothing left to run
  # (`at_idle`, before the scheduler waits) or has passed `LATE_STEPS`
  # points and back-edges since: the latest an OS lets it in, on every
  # seed (bench/std_mutex_exercise.sh). The step bound keeps a program
  # that spins for the thread from waiting for ever, as no OS keeps a
  # thread out for ever. The word is an `Atomic`'s, read and written here
  # only, the runtime's, so not a point; the simulated thread is its only
  # writer.
  private def self.late_word : Pointer(Atomic(UInt64))
    Pointer(Atomic(UInt64)).new(pointerof(@@late_closed).address)
  end

  # In `IyiThread.start`, before the thread exists.
  def self.hold_start : Nil
    return unless @@late_threads && @@mode == SIMULATED && @@here
    @@late_steps = 0_u64
    late_word.value.set(1_u64)
  end

  # On the started thread, before it links itself: nothing here touches
  # the heap, which no stop scans for this thread yet.
  def self.wait_late : Nil
    return unless @@late_threads
    while late_word.value.get != 0_u64
      IyiThread.yield_cpu
    end
  end

  # The simulated thread has nothing to run: a thread held is let in.
  def self.at_idle : Nil
    late_word.value.set(0_u64) if @@late_closed != 0_u64 && @@mode == SIMULATED && @@here
  end

  private def self.late_tick : Nil
    @@late_steps = @@late_steps &+ 1_u64
    late_word.value.set(0_u64) if @@late_steps >= LATE_STEPS
  end

  # ── The end ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  # With `IYI_CHAOS_TRACE` set: the seed, the strategy and the schedule,
  # on standard error as the program ends (`__iyi_flush_std`), once.
  def self.report : Nil
    return unless @@trace && !@@reported && active?
    @@reported = true
    strategy = @@pct ? "pct depth #{@@depth} over #{@@horizon} steps" : "random walk 1 in #{@@odds}"
    text = if @@mode == SIMULATED
             "iyi chaos: seed #{@@seed}, #{strategy}, #{@@steps} points, #{@@yields} preemptions, #{@@picks} choices, schedule #{@@schedule.to_s(16)}\n"
           else
             "iyi chaos: seed #{@@seed}, #{strategy}, real threads: no schedule to name\n"
           end
    __iyi_write(2, text.to_unsafe.as(Void*), text.bytesize.to_u64)
  end
end

class IyiWorkers
  # The back-edge word of this thread raised, for the simulation: the
  # thread-local, or on x86-64 Windows the TEB slot, which is
  # `ArbitraryUserPointer` while no pool has claimed one - and none does
  # under the simulation, which starts no pool.
  def self.chaos_raise : Nil
    {% if flag?(:win32) && flag?(:x86_64) && !flag?(:preempt_check_accessor) %}
      Pointer(UInt64).new(IyiRoots.current_teb &+ @@preempt_slot).value = 1_u64
    {% else %}
      @@preempt = 1_u64
    {% end %}
  end

  def self.chaos_give_up(st : IyiSchedulerState, fiber : IyiFiber) : Nil
    give_up(st, fiber)
  end
end

class IyiScheduler
  # `wake_on` with the waiters chosen from the stream: up to *count* of
  # those parked on *word*, each drawn from the ones left, readied in the
  # order drawn. A draw of 0 each time is the plain wake's oldest-first.
  # The ones left are counted and the drawn one found by walking the
  # bucket, not gathered into an array: an array made here is the
  # waker's partition's, and names waiters of other units (heap22), which
  # the verifier reads as a foreign partition's chunk held from this one
  # once their unit dies.
  def self.chaos_wake_on(word : Pointer(Atomic(UInt64)), count : Int32) : Nil
    heads = @@lot_heads
    tails = @@lot_tails
    return unless heads.is_a?(Array(IyiWaiter?)) && tails.is_a?(Array(IyiWaiter?))
    bucket = lot_bucket(word.address)
    lock = lot_lock(bucket)
    IyiChanLock.lock(lock)
    left = 0
    node = heads[bucket]
    while node.is_a?(IyiWaiter)
      left = left + 1 if node.slot == word.address
      node = node.next_node
    end
    woken = 0
    chain : IyiFiber? = nil
    last : IyiFiber? = nil
    while woken < count && left > 0
      index = IyiChaos.below(left)
      chosen = heads[bucket]
      while chosen.is_a?(IyiWaiter) && (chosen.slot != word.address || index > 0)
        index = index - 1 if chosen.slot == word.address
        chosen = chosen.next_node
      end
      break unless chosen.is_a?(IyiWaiter)
      left = left - 1
      lot_unlink(heads, tails, bucket, chosen)
      if chosen.claim
        fiber = chosen.fiber
        fiber.next_run = nil
        if last.is_a?(IyiFiber)
          last.next_run = fiber
        else
          chain = fiber
        end
        last = fiber
        woken = woken + 1
      end
    end
    IyiChanLock.unlock(lock)
    while chain.is_a?(IyiFiber)
      following = chain.next_run
      ready(chain, false)
      chain = following
    end
  end
end
